@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple SysML activity with 5-6 actions and one decision.
'   usecase:      Teach action, control flow, decision/merge with continuous-flow note.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       systems-engineering
' ============================================================================
title Example SysML Activity - Simple Control Flow

' SysML activity = UML activity extended with continuous/discrete flow concepts.
' Use !theme plain or default; here we stay stock for portability.

|System|
start
' A plain action node. In SysML these may be invoked behaviors or ops.
:Read Setpoint;
:Measure Process Variable;
:Compute Error;
if (Error > Threshold?) then (yes)
  :Actuate Valve;
else (no)
  :Hold Position;
  ' Merge node — the two branches rejoin here, shown implicitly by
  ' the shared control flow to the next action.
endif
:Log State;
stop

' SysML extension point — a note flagging that this same flow can carry
' a continuous stereotype in streaming variants (see medium example).
note right of Measure Process Variable
  <b>SysML note:</b>
  This flow is discrete here.
  Add «continuous» for
  streaming sensors.
end note

@enduml
